  "notes": "Warm off-white (#f6f5f2) app canvas with two white rounded (12px) panels. Signature element: tiny pill chips (999px radius, 10px/600) overlaid inline on the PDF text, each colour-coded by visualization type — pink=3D model, lavender=formula, blue=graph, green=source, amber=animation — with a type icon and truncated label; the selected chip gets a dark outline and a tooltip. Clicking a chip swaps the right Visualizer panel (graph, KaTeX-style formula derivation with numbered steps, etc.). The panel header shows a type pill matching chip colour. The Visualizer dropdown is actually a mode switcher (Knowledge Graph, Chat, Flashcards, Quizzes, Feynman) with descriptive menu items. Floating white pill toolbars for page nav and zoom sit at the bottom of the document pane. In the tall capture the chip overlay positions drift relative to the canvas text; DOM bboxes used."
